title: Binary Star
text: One white laser, two stars. Each shines one way on the square and another on the slant, and the far one has them the other way round.
trick: a star fed square-on fires only diagonals, but one of its own diagonal rays sent back through a green filter by a head-on mirror makes it fire a green cross too. So the near star runs white on the slant and green on the square; its green east ray and a white diagonal ray (turned by a mirror that also carries the far star back) strike the far star, which comes out the other way round: white on the square, green on the slant
motif: a binary star: two stars on one line, each drawn by the open rays around it in a field of occupied squares; a feed lane below
expect: reversals>=1
---
L 0 11 2 w
*R 4 11 1 k
*Z 4 7 0 k
*F 5 6 3 g
*R 7 4 7 k
*R 7 10 2 k
*Z 10 7 0 k
